# Data writes — Calling CRM

## Local DB — always allowed (no ask)

When `MONGO_URL` / backend `.env` targets **local Mongo** (e.g. `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, local Docker), the agent **must** run verification that writes without waiting for permission:

- Backend **pytest** (`pytest tests/…`, full suite)
- Starting/restarting the local API (including lifespan `ensure_*` master upserts)
- Browser QA that creates/updates/deletes **tagged** `TEST_*` records on local DB, with teardown when tests define it

Do **not** skip pytest or browser because “it writes to Mongo” when the DB is local.

## Remote / production — ask first

Stop and get an explicit yes before any write when the target is:

- Atlas or any non-local `MONGO_URL` (including values from `deploy/.env`)
- Cutover `--apply`, wipe scripts, bulk import/seed against shared/live data
- Creating untagged dummy business data outside pytest teardown patterns

## Still ask (even on local)

- Destructive wipes / drop database
- Cutover apply or one-off migration `--apply` against large real datasets
- Anything aimed at a remote URI

## Allowed always (any env)

- Read-only inspection (`GET`, Mongo find, logs)
- Editing source or test **code**
- Frontend RTL tests that mock the API and do not hit Mongo

## Examples

```text
# GOOD — local .env → run without asking
pytest tests/backend_test.py -v --tb=short
npm run dev   # ensure_* upserts on boot

# BAD — skip local pytest “waiting on permission”
"Backend pytest will write… Run it?"

# BAD — unsolicited writes to Atlas / deploy Mongo
pytest against deploy/.env Atlas without explicit yes
```
